@format 1
@id media-preview.common.backend-failure
@title Backend current failure
@section Media preview
@area Common
@entry fail-request
@summary Trace LMediaLoadFailCurrent, including the second generation/disposal check that can turn an apparent current failure into an obsolete result.
@related media-preview.common.backend-load, media-preview.common.completion-routing
@tag media
@tag preview
@tag common
@tag failure

@alias media-load = Cadroue.Media.LMediaLoad

[fail-request] Backend failure helper requested <input>
~ This starts with background loader failure helper requested.
[Technical explanation]
= Source validation or a reader exception has reached LMediaLoadFailCurrent with the request generation and path.
> fail-current

[fail-current] Failure helper ownership recheck <decision>
~ The program checks again that the failed read still belongs to the current request.
[Technical explanation]
- Under the backend gate, recheck disposal and request generation before clearing pending state and constructing the requested failure/cancellation outcome @ media-load.LMediaLoadFailCurrent(...)
? "Request became obsolete" > obsolete
? "Request still current" > fail-raised

[obsolete] Failure became obsolete <output>
~ The failure belongs to an older request, so it is ignored.
[Technical explanation]
= LMediaLoadFailCurrent returns LMediaLoadObsolete and does not raise LMediaLoadCompleted.

[fail-raised] Current failure/cancellation raised <process>
~ This step handles current failure/cancellation raised.
[Technical explanation]
- Raise the current failure/cancellation outcome to each LMediaLoadCompleted subscriber individually @ media-load.LMediaLoadFailCurrent(...)
  @ media-load.LMediaLoadRaise(...)
> map:media-preview.common.completion-routing
